From 46f9e8e44b41172abff56d19b94fa0d45258d5bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 00:15:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 145/162] feat: rec_CaptureEXR sequences no longer overwrite
 the previous take (r_SceneReferredExportSequenceNaming)

User: a second sequence into the same folder and prefix wrote frame.000000.exr over the first.
Single frames already continued from the first free number on disk; sequences restarted at
zero on every arm. New cvar r_SceneReferredExportSequenceNaming: 0 = restart at zero (the
original), 1 = continue from the first free <prefix>.%06d.exr in the folder (default), 2 = the
prefix gains _YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS and numbering starts at zero. The "capture armed" log line now
says which number the take starts from. ConsoleReference.md updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HXzRVK4yBVDUNfdWXEwV5y
