@@ -336,6 +338,13 @@ Two existing cvars change what they mean while the switch is on:
   instead. `r_HDREyeAdaptationMode` likewise stops selecting anything - the scene-referred branch
   is chosen ahead of it, which is the point of S0's D14 work.
 
+### r_SceneReferredExportSequenceNaming
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Default | 1 |
+| Purpose | How a **sequence** from `rec_CaptureEXR` is numbered (single frames always continue from the first free number on disk). **0** restarts at `000000` on every arm - the original behaviour, and a second take into the same folder and prefix overwrites the first. **1 = continue**: start at the first free `<prefix>.%06d.exr` in the folder; nothing on disk is overwritten and takes number on. **2 = timestamp**: the prefix becomes `<prefix>_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS` and numbering starts at zero - one folder, one sub-name per take. The armed line in the log says which number the take starts from. |
